WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.310
We know that Thanos's Infinity Gauntlet is
going to be making a return in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.660
The only question is just what's going to
happen with it.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.330
Will one of the heroes manage to take the
Infinity Gauntlet and use its incredible power

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:12.920
for themselves?

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.600
Here's why these superheroes might wear the
Infinity Gauntlet in Endgame.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.060
If there's one character you actually want
to see controlling the Infinity Stones and

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:25.270
the omnipotent power that goes along with
them, it's Steve Rogers, the guy who always

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.960
does the right thing, no matter what.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.660
"We may not be perfect, but the safest hands
are still our own."

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.740
If he got his hands on the Gauntlet, then
it's easy to see how all of that death and

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.190
destruction at the end of Infinity War could
be corrected, he'd set things right again

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.440
even if there was a huge cost to doing so,
which there almost certainly would be.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.421
When Thanos uses the Infinity Gauntlet at
the end of Infinity War, we see that the gauntlet

00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:51.780
itself is burnt out and damaged, nearly shattered
by the forces that it channeled.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.460
That's no mean feat considering that it was
crafted by the same dwarves who crafted Mjolnir,

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.880
which took a literal goddess of death to break.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.480
Thanos survived the Gauntlet's power surge,
but he's also an incredibly powerful Titan.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:08.350
Captain America can run faster than a luxury
vehicle, leap off rooftops, and bicep curl

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.220
a helicopter, and he's the moral fiber that
holds the Avengers together.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.240
"S—- … Language!"

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:20.680
His indomitable will would no doubt give him
the ability to use the Gauntlet, but surviving

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.229
it is a different question.

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:26.659
The backlash in controlling those forces and
unwinding time to make things right would

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:30.940
give him the perfect opportunity for the heroic
sacrifice that would bring the character to

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:34.240
the end that Chris Evans and the Russo brothers
have been hinting at.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.900
Tony Stark might not seem like the prime candidate
to wear the Gauntlet, but if you think about

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.620
it, he fits, wait for it, like a glove.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.780
After all, for all its mystical sci-fi trappings,
the Gauntlet is just another piece of technology,

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.700
and technology is Iron Man's specialty.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.980
"When did you become an expert in thermonuclear
astrophysics?

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:52.880
… Last night."

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.780
All this happened in the comic books already.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:59.730
He's actually the first human in the Marvel
Universe to wield the Gauntlet, a relatively

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.380
recent event that happened in the pages of
Avengers in 2011.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:07.940
One of the most interesting things about that
is what Tony does with it: he creates an illusion

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.810
of the Gauntlet being destroyed, but then
secretly hands off the Stones to the people

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.720
he trusts most.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.219
Of course, all that stuff about heroic sacrifice
still applies to Tony, and this may give us

00:02:17.219 --> 00:02:22.060
a fond farewell to Robert Downey Jr., allowing
Jim Rhodes to step into the armor as the new

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:22.800
Iron Man.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.920
"Merry Christmas, buddy."

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.620
The most likely character to wear the Infinity
Gauntlet in Endgame might also be the most

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.120
surprising, at least for MCU fans who haven't
checked out the source material.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:37.820
Thanos daughter Nebula played a critical role to the Infinity Gauntlet storyline

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:42.120
in the comics, and given what happened to
Gamora in Infinity War, she has the personal

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.240
motivation too.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.760
In the original Infinity Gauntlet storyline,
Thanos' murder of half the universe isn't

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.440
his climactic goal, it's his opening move.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.420
When the surviving heroes head out to the
edge of the universe, Thanos brutally destroys

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.540
them one by one.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.160
All the while, Nebula is there watching, trapped
in a desiccated corpse and kept on the edge

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.700
of life and death just to amuse Thanos.

00:03:02.769 --> 00:03:06.940
There is, however, enough consciousness left
in her that she's able to eventually steal

00:03:06.949 --> 00:03:12.199
the gauntlet when Thanos abandons his body,
and shifts the timeline back by 24 hours,

00:03:12.199 --> 00:03:15.340
before Thanos snapped his fingers and killed
off the heroes.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.440
If the movies go a similar way, that could
add a very personal element to the struggle

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.449
against Thanos.

00:03:20.449 --> 00:03:25.010
In the movies, Nebula has been tortured her
entire life, her body replaced piece by piece

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.699
with cybernetics as punishment for her "failures,"
leaving her in the disassembled state that

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.040
we see in Infinity War.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.600
She's already vowed to hunt him down and return
the favor.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.240
"...yeah."

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:49.269
Not only that, but Gamora, the "sister" who
tried to protect her, was murdered by Thanos.

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:53.760
If Gamora stays dead, Nebula's vengeance on
Thanos would be very satisfying, and could

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.269
even set her up to join the Guardians, bonding
with Star-Lord over the loss of Gamora.

00:03:58.269 --> 00:04:02.840
"Well, well … You should have killed me
… It would have been a waste of parts."

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.919
Bruce Banner might just be the most compelling
choice to get control of the Infinity Gauntlet

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:09.560
in Endgame.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.859
Since Thor: Ragnarok, we've seen the Hulk
at war with his alter ego, and in Infinity

00:04:13.859 --> 00:04:17.920
War, that was compounded when the greener
side of Banner's personality refused to come

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.180
out and fight, even when the world was at
stake.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.620
"Dude you're embarrassing me in front of the wizard."

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:33.380
If Banner does take control of the Gauntlet,
he might use it to finally find the harmony

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:37.780
between the warring factions of his psyche
that he's been looking for since he was created.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:42.030
That could give us another element of the
comics: a unified version of the Hulk who

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.040
has the gamma-powered body of the Green Goliath,
and the brilliant mind of Bruce Banner.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:50.290
We could get quite a bit out of the idea of
Banner controlling the Infinity Gauntlet,

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:55.500
including a chance for Mark Ruffalo to do
some Hulk acting that wasn't limited to monosyllabes

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.100
and smashing.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:56.980
"I Smash you"

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.200
"yeah yeah, sure."

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.160
Baby arms.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:04:59.920
what?

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:01.270
"baby!"

00:05:02.289 --> 00:05:06.760
The God of Thunder armed with both the unstoppable
Stormbreaker and the Infinity Gauntlet is

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.820
pretty much the definition of "overpowered."

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.840
We'll admit that this seems like a pretty
unlikely scenario, but believe it or not,

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.820
something similar happened in the comics.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:24.450
Way back in 2000's Thor #25, the God of Thunder
took on Thanos in one of the most brutal fights

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.580
to hit the comics page.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.440
While Thanos was winning at first, Thor geared
up with a whole new set of mystical artifacts

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:35.330
enchanted by Odin, and wound up beating the
purple out of the Mad Titan until he was face-down

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.820
in the Asgardian dirt.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.700
Unlikely, yes, but also pretty rad.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.000
Loki, in case you forgot, is dead.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.740
He was killed in the opening scenes of Infinity
War, murdered by Thanos after trying to save

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.560
the brother he spent so much of his time luring
into hilarious stabbings.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:54.100
"He transformed himself into a snake and he
knows that I love snakes so I went to pick

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:57.560
up the snake to admire it and he transformed
back into himself and went “blah!

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:58.720
It’s me!” and he stabbed me."

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:03.860
That said, death has never exactly stopped
Loki before, so why would it be a problem

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:04.360
now?

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.340
Coming back from the dead is what the dude
does, and a last-second revival and a theft

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.410
of the Infinity Gauntlet might just tip the
scales in Endgame.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:15.020
You’re not going to believe this one, but
it kinda happened before in the comics…

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:15.900
kinda.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:21.220
In the original Infinity Gauntlet comic, Thanos
is paired up with Mephisto, a demon who eventually

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.230
betrays him.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:25.600
The thing is, Mephisto doesn't currently exist
in the MCU.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:30.330
Instead, the role of a lackey who eventually
betrays Thanos has actually fallen to Loki.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.270
Plus, we already know that there's a Loki
TV show in development, with Tom Hiddleston

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.280
attached to star.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:39.420
Unless it's a prequel, he's definitely coming
back in some form or another.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:43.790
If he gains control of the Infinity Gauntlet
and somehow manages to resist the corrupting

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:48.140
influence of absolute power, that could complete
the shift in his character from unrepentant

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:52.930
villain to devious antihero, exactly what
he needs to be if he's going to be a protagonist

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:53.920
from here on out.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.920
The trailer for Endgame is relentlessly depressing,
full of stuff like Tony Stark recording his

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:03.450
final message to Pepper, Steve Rogers shedding
tears over the fate of his friends, and Clint

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.200
Barton looking haunted in the rain.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.600
That is, until the very end, when Ant-Man
shows up and suddenly things are as goofy

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:10.280
as they've ever been.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.740
"Can you buzz me in?"

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:17.120
Scott Lang getting his hands on the Infinity
Gauntlet would be pretty shocking, but it's

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.430
not entirely unlikely.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:22.940
The entire Marvel Universe is about the little
guy managing to triumph over impossible odds.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:26.880
In both a figurative and literal sense, there's
no littler guy than Ant-Man.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.540
It's also his chance to actually save the
world.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.160
One of the fun things about the Ant-Man films
is that they have smaller stakes than the

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.440
rest of the MCU.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.160
Getting him involved in something this big
would be weird and wild enough to be really

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:38.840
fun.

